================================================================================
  Lead game server installed.

  The post-install step has already (best effort):
    * created the 'lead' user/group
    * built the runtime tree + symlinks under /var/db/lead
    * enabled & started MariaDB and created the databases + migrations
    * enabled the service (lead_enable=YES)

  BEFORE STARTING, set the address clients connect to. Edit the public/bind IP
  in the core configs (these are @config files, preserved across upgrades):

      /usr/local/etc/lead/auth/CONFIG
      /usr/local/etc/lead/channel1/game1/CONFIG   (and game2, channel99)
      /usr/local/etc/lead/db/conf.txt

  Then start everything:

      service lead start
      service lead status

  Re-run the DB bootstrap any time (idempotent; applies new migrations):

      /usr/local/libexec/lead/lead-db-setup

  Update later (downloads the matching FreeBSD/arch .pkg from the GitHub release
  and upgrades in place only if newer; --check just compares versions):

      /usr/local/libexec/lead/lead-update

  Logs live under /var/db/lead/<core>/{syserr.txt,log/}.
================================================================================
